version 3. The full text travels with them: it is served by this site at
/LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt, and sits at ../../LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt relative to this
notice.

They are a MODIFIED version of the world border snapshots published by
aourednik/historical-basemaps (https://github.com/aourednik/historical-basemaps),
copyright its authors.

This is the same data as ../years/, kept at a higher resolution. The coarse tier
is what the map draws when the whole world is on screen; these files replace it
once the view is close enough that the simplified coastline would be visibly
faceted. Both tiers come out of the same build, from the same sources, under the
same licence.

What was changed: each snapshot was simplified with mapshaper (Visvalingam,
keep-shapes on so that small polities do not vanish) and converted to TopoJSON,
which also removes the duplication where two neighbours share a border. One file
per year. Nothing about the geometry was invented, corrected or re-attributed.

The corresponding source is the upstream project linked above, together with
../../../scripts/fetch-borders.mjs and ../../../scripts/build-borders.mjs.

The application that draws these files is NOT under this licence — see LICENSE
at the root. It contains none of this data; it fetches these files at runtime
and would draw any other dataset in the same format.
